Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02  
  – "project_short_name": filter rows to the bladder cancer cohort (`'TCGA-BLCA'`).  
  – "Hugo_Symbol": locate mutations in the gene of interest (e.g. `CDKN2A`).  
  – "case_barcode": patient‑level ID to join with both clinical and RNA‑Seq tables.  

• TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39  
  – "project_short_name": secondary check that samples belong to `TCGA-BLCA`.  
  – "gene_name": select the four target genes (`MDM2, TP53, CDKN1A, CCNE1`).  
  – "tpm_unstranded" (or "fpkm_unstranded", "fpkm_uq_unstranded"): RNA expression value.  
  – "case_barcode": join key to somatic‑mutation and clinical tables.  
  – "sample_type_name": restrict to “Primary Tumor” or inspect other sample categories.  

• TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.CLINICAL_GDC_R39  
  – "submitter_id": clinical‑level patient ID (same human‑readable format as "case_barcode").  
  – "primary_site", "disease_type", "diag__primary_diagnosis": clinical cancer descriptors.  
  – "demo__gender", "demo__race", "demo__vital_status", "diag__year_of_diagnosis", … : useful clinical‑metadata columns to accompany expression results.  

Typical conditions that will be useful  
• "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA' (bladder cancer).  
• "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A' (identify mutated patients).  
• "gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1').  
• Joining key: SOMATIC.case_barcode  =  CLINICAL.submitter_id  
               SOMATIC.case_barcode  =  RNA.case_barcode.  
• Optional: "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Primary%Tumor%' to look only at primary tumors.  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that move from simple inspection to a complete answer.  
Every identifier is enclosed in double quotes as required.

```sql
-- 1. Description:  List all distinct projects that appear in the mutation table.
SELECT DISTINCT "project_short_name"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description:  Look at mutation records for CDKN2A in bladder cancer and preview the barcodes.
SELECT DISTINCT
       "case_barcode",
       "sample_barcode_tumor",
       "Variant_Classification"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description:  Count how many unique bladder‑cancer cases carry a CDKN2A mutation.
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT "case_barcode") AS "num_cdkn2a_mut_cases"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A';
```

```sql
-- 4. Description:  Inspect RNA‑Seq rows for BLCA samples for one target gene (MDM2) to confirm column content.
SELECT DISTINCT
       "case_barcode",
       "sample_barcode",
       "gene_name",
       "tpm_unstranded",
       "sample_type_name"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND "gene_name" = 'MDM2'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description:  Pull RNA expression of the four genes for all BLCA samples (no mutation filter yet).
SELECT
       "case_barcode",
       "gene_name",
       "tpm_unstranded"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND "gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description:  Get expression of the four genes only in cases that have a CDKN2A mutation (join via case_barcode).
WITH cdkn2a_mut_cases AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
    FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02"
    WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
      AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
)
SELECT r."case_barcode",
       r."gene_name",
       r."tpm_unstranded",
       r."sample_barcode",
       r."sample_type_name"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39" r
JOIN cdkn2a_mut_cases m
  ON r."case_barcode" = m."case_barcode"
WHERE r."gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description:  Bring in a few clinical columns for the same patients.
WITH cdkn2a_mut_cases AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
    FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02"
    WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
      AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
)
SELECT r."case_barcode",
       r."gene_name",
       r."tpm_unstranded",
       c."primary_site",
       c."disease_type",
       c."demo__gender",
       c."demo__race",
       c."demo__vital_status"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39" r
JOIN cdkn2a_mut_cases m
  ON r."case_barcode" = m."case_barcode"
LEFT JOIN "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."CLINICAL_GDC_R39" c
  ON m."case_barcode" = c."submitter_id"
WHERE r."gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description:  Restrict to primary‑tumor RNA samples and display year of diagnosis.
WITH cdkn2a_mut_cases AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
    FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02"
    WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
      AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
)
SELECT r."case_barcode",
       r."gene_name",
       r."tpm_unstranded",
       c."diag__year_of_diagnosis",
       c."demo__gender",
       r."sample_barcode"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39" r
JOIN cdkn2a_mut_cases m
  ON r."case_barcode" = m."case_barcode"
LEFT JOIN "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."CLINICAL_GDC_R39" c
  ON m."case_barcode" = c."submitter_id"
WHERE r."gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')
  AND r."sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Primary%Tumor%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description:  Compute the mean TPM per gene across CDKN2A‑mutated bladder cancers.
WITH cdkn2a_mut_cases AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
    FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02"
    WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
      AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
)
SELECT r."gene_name",
       AVG(r."tpm_unstranded") AS "avg_tpm"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39" r
JOIN cdkn2a_mut_cases m
  ON r."case_barcode" = m."case_barcode"
WHERE r."gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')
GROUP BY r."gene_name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description:  Final report combining clinical info with a pivot‑style layout (one row per case).
WITH cdkn2a_mut_cases AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
    FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02"
    WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
      AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
),
expr AS (
    SELECT "case_barcode",
           "gene_name",
           "tpm_unstranded"
    FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39"
    WHERE "gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')
      AND "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Primary%Tumor%'
)
SELECT c."submitter_id"          AS "case_barcode",
       MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MDM2'   THEN e."tpm_unstranded" END) AS "MDM2_TPM",
       MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'TP53'   THEN e."tpm_unstranded" END) AS "TP53_TPM",
       MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'CDKN1A' THEN e."tpm_unstranded" END) AS "CDKN1A_TPM",
       MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'CCNE1'  THEN e."tpm_unstranded" END) AS "CCNE1_TPM",
       c."demo__gender",
       c."demo__vital_status",
       c."diag__year_of_diagnosis"
FROM cdkn2a_mut_cases m
LEFT JOIN "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."CLINICAL_GDC_R39" c
  ON m."case_barcode" = c."submitter_id"
LEFT JOIN expr e
  ON m."case_barcode" = e."case_barcode"
GROUP BY c."submitter_id",
         c."demo__gender",
         c."demo__vital_status",
         c."diag__year_of_diagnosis"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries progressively explore the data needed to answer the question and culminate in a concise joined view of RNA expression and clinical characteristics for bladder‑cancer patients harboring CDKN2A mutations.
